/* ProxyMirror Help interface text. Keep keys stable; translate only values. */
"automation_content" = "Scripts run in a separate worker with execution limits. Filter Console by errors, warnings, user or system logs. Save and enable with Command-S; format with Command-B. require supports built-in modules and controlled local Addons, rather than a complete Node filesystem or npm installer. Reset sharedState from the scripting window.\n\nFind MCP connection configuration in Help. HTTP listens on loopback with a per-launch token; stdio uses proxymirror-cli mcp stdio. Continue incremental queries from the last flow ID.";
"backup_folder" = "Backup Folder";
"clear_rebuildable_caches_as_with_a_macos_memory_warning" = "Clear rebuildable caches as with a macOS memory warning; preserve captured records, sessions and user files";
"copy_debug_information" = "Copy Debug Information";
"data_backups" = "Data & Backups";
"data_content" = "Use File > Save Session for an active session and Saved Folders for important requests. Clearing the capture list does not export a session. Request retention and body limits control memory; bytes that were never captured cannot be recovered.\n\nRule/settings backups include tool configuration and Protobuf descriptors. Keep private keys and Keychain tokens separately. Restoring defaults first saves a rule backup in Backups. Preview a backup before merging or replacing it. Open saved sessions from File > Open.";
"data_folder" = "Data Folder";
"device_connection_failed" = "Device Connection Failed…";
"device_setup" = "Device Setup";
"devices_content" = "In Advanced Proxy Settings, select the Mac LAN listening address, add the device IP or CIDR allowlist and apply it. The device must be able to reach the Mac; configure its proxy with the selected Mac address and listening port. Install and trust this Mac's CA on the device for HTTPS.\n\nAndroid Emulator can reach the host loopback through 10.0.2.2. Whether an application trusts user CAs depends on its debug network security configuration. See the Certificate menu for platform and framework guides.";
"documentation_feedback" = "Documentation & Feedback";
"getting_started" = "Getting Started";
"getting_started_content" = "1. Start the listener and check its port in the status bar.\n2. Enable the macOS system proxy, or configure your test client to use http://127.0.0.1:%ld.\n3. For HTTPS inspection, install and trust the CA, then enable MITM and the appropriate SSL rules.\n4. Send a test request and inspect its body, raw message, timings and connection log.\n5. Restore the system proxy and stop listening when finished.";
"https_certificates" = "HTTPS & Certificates";
"https_content" = "After installing the CA, check its trust in Keychain Access, expiry date and fingerprint. Global MITM, SSL Proxying List, application rules, excluded hosts and tool switches determine whether new connections are decrypted. Reconnect the client after changing them.\n\nIf the client rejects the test CA or uses certificate pinning, choose passthrough for its application or domain. Passthrough records tunnel metadata only. Resetting the CA requires clients to trust the new certificate; existing captured sessions are preserved.";
